# transient / large / machine-specific outputs (keep .json summaries + .pdf figures)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
artifacts/*.log
artifacts/*.npz
artifacts/*.tipsy
artifacts/bonsai*
# the nested per-run dirs hold the shared ICs and per-theta force dumps (tens of MB);
# the top-level *.json summaries are the durable record and stay tracked
artifacts/**/*.tipsy
artifacts/**/*.npz
# profiler traces (1.3 GB) and HLO dumps are regenerable and far too large to track
artifacts/traces/
artifacts/grad/*.txt
# per-run logs: the .json rows are the record. The exception is artifacts/probes/,
# where the logs ARE the evidence (the pkdgrav3-track probes print, they do not write rows)
artifacts/**/*.log
!artifacts/probes/*.log
